  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think there has to be awareness for the many functionalities of clients that are out there and that we really need a reliable system that has to exceed the current reporting possibilities by far.\nDraft of how this could be working:\nA button in the selected users menu to mark the person as malicious/harmful (or another word suggesting hacking/crashing etc. users). After clicking the button the user will first be blocked if not already done. It will also ask other users in the lobby if the user is perceived as hacker/crasher. In the next step, the following functions/informations will only be processed on server-side, so hackers can't abuse them so easily: One account can mark a person as this kind of malicious user only one time. The server will give the user that has sent the vote a feedback on whether the vote has been received or not. That's important because it tells us if the hacker actually avoided the transmission of the information somehow, because there are clients preventing all sorts of things from actually happening. Voting someone as malicious will be counted on vrc servers. If the count exceeds a critical amount in a certain amount of time it will ban the account from vrchat.",
